背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"16b78196\" lines=\"6-20\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:12:Assemble colored sprites into a central bar's notches, chaining successive pieces along fixed-width strips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:14:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:15:- bg = most common color. Largest monochrome component is a solid \"bar\" with boundary notches (bg holes opening to its bbox edge).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:16:- Several smaller colored sprites scattered around the bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:17:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:18:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:19:- Each bar notch is filled by a root piece whose shape exactly covers the hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:20:- The root defines a strip (column-span or row-span) for its chain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:21:- Successive pieces fill the bg cells inside the previous piece's bbox, locked to the same strip width.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:22:- Multiple chains grow independently from different bar notches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:23:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:24:Key insight: The root piece's extent perpendicular to the chain direction locks the strip width for all subsequent pieces in that chain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:25:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:26:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:27:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:28:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b0039139\" lines=\"29-44\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:29:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:30:Recolor a cropped template and repeat it according to a component-count stencil.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:31:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:32:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:33:- Solid blue (1) separator rows or columns split the grid into four sections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:34:- Section 1 is a black-background shape template; section 2 is a component-count stencil.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:35:- Sections 3 and 4 are solid color swatches for output foreground and background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:36:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:37:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:38:- Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black pixels and recolor it with the two swatches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:39:- Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:40:- Repeat the recolored crop that many times, inserting one background-colored row/column between copies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:41:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:42:Key insight: The second section encodes only the repeat count; the output orientation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:43:is inherited from whether the input separators are columns or rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:44:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:45:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:46:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:47:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\" lines=\"9-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:48:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:49:Slide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:50:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:51:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:52:- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:53:- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:54:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:55:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:56:- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:57:- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:58:- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:59:- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:60:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:61:Key insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:62:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:63:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:64:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:65:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2ba387bc\" lines=\"6-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:66:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:67:Sort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:68:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:69:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:70:- bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:71:- Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:72:- Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:73:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:74:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:75:- Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:76:- Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:77:- Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:78:- Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:79:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:80:Key insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:81:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:82:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:83:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:84:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"6e453dd6\" lines=\"39-52\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:85:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:86:Slide black shapes rightward to a grey separator, then shoot red rays from enclosed holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:87:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:88:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:89:- A vertical grey (5) separator column divides the grid into left and right halves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:90:- Black shapes sit on the left side against a background color (bg).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:91:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:92:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:93:- Translate each black connected component rightward until its right edge is flush with the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:94:- After sliding, find enclosed bg regions (holes) within the black shapes that touch the column just left of the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:95:- For each row spanned by such a hole, emit a red ray across the entire right half of the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:96:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:97:Key insight: Only holes adjacent to the separator trigger rays — the sliding creates enclosures that act as \"nozzles\" projecting rightward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:98:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:99:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:100:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:101:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"291dc1e1\" lines=\"7-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:102:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:103:Reorder and stack rectangles by proximity to two colored edge lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:104:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:105:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:106:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:107:- Two edge lines (h + v) meet at a corner marked by a unique color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:108:- \"Blue\" line is color 1 if present, else the longer line; other is \"red.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:109:- Solid rectangles in the interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:110:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:111:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:112:- Sort rectangles by (distance to blue edge, distance to red edge).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:113:- If the blue edge is vertical, rotate each rectangle 90° CCW.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:114:- Stack top-to-bottom, centered horizontally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:115:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:116:Key insight: Edge-line colors encode a coordinate system; proximity to each axis determines stacking order and rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:117:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:118:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:119:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:120:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"e376de54\" lines=\"41-55\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:121:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:122:Align parallel colored line segments so they all share the same start and end positions as a reference line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:123:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:124:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:125:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:126:- Several parallel line segments (diagonal, horizontal, or vertical), each a different color, running in the same direction but starting/ending at different positions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:127:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:128:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:129:- Detect the dominant direction shared by all segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:130:- Pick the median segment (by perpendicular offset) as the reference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:131:- Shift every segment along the shared direction so its start aligns with the reference's start, then trim or extend it to match the reference's length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:132:- Grid size stays the same; isolated single pixels are untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:133:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:134:Key insight: The reference is the median line, not the longest; all segments are snapped to its extent regardless of their original length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:135:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:136:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:137:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:138:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"981571dc\" lines=\"6-19\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:139:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:140:Reconstruct a 4-way symmetric mosaic by filling missing (black) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:141:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:142:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:143:- A colored grid exhibiting bilateral symmetry along both a vertical and a horizontal axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:144:- Some pixels are erased to color 0 (black), creating gaps in the pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:145:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:146:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:147:- Infer the vertical and horizontal reflection axes from the visible (non-zero) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:148:- For each black pixel, recover its color from the mirrored position across either axis or both.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:149:- When multiple mirrors yield candidates, use the majority color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:150:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:151:Key insight: The reflection axes are not given — they must be deduced from the surviving pixels by finding the axes that best preserve the existing symmetry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:152:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:153:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:154:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:155:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"38007db0\" lines=\"9-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:156:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:157:Extract the unique cell from each lattice row into a single-column lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:158:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:159:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:160:- Grid divided into equal square cells by uniform gridlines of color L.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:161:- Cell interiors filled with bg; each cell has an inner sprite pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:162:- Each row of cells has exactly one cell with a unique pattern; the rest are copies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:163:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:164:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:165:- For each lattice row, find the cell whose inner pattern appears exactly once (the \"odd one out\").\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:166:- Construct a single-column lattice preserving the original row heights, containing only the unique cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:167:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:168:Key insight: The task is per-row \"odd one out\" — every cell in a row is identical except one oddball, which must be extracted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:169:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:170:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:171:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:172:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"1ae2feb7\" lines=\"30-45\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:173:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:174:Extend row bars periodically across the opposite side of a separator column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:175:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:176:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:177:- bg = background. A near-solid vertical separator divides the grid into two sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:178:- One side contains horizontal colored bars; the other side is blank target space.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:179:- Bars may be stacked by row and may sit at different distances from the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:180:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:181:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:182:- Identify the separator as the column whose non-bg cells are one color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:183:- Treat the denser side as the bar side and collect each contiguous row run.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:184:- Process bars from nearest to farthest from the separator; for each bar, paint its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:185:  color every bar-length cells into the blank side without overwriting earlier paint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:186:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:187:Key insight: Each bar's length is the period for its extension, and nearer bars claim target cells first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:188:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:189:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:190:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:191:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"9bbf930d\" lines=\"61-72\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:192:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:193:Move magenta particles along corridors formed by parallel colored bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:194:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:195:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:196:- bg=7. Particles=6 in col 0. Colored bars on even rows form corridors on odd rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:197:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:198:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:199:- Particle goes straight through bg cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:200:- When blocked by a colored cell, turns 90° into the perpendicular direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:201:  that has a bg cell flanked by same-color bars. Stops at grid edge or full blockage.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:202:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:203:Key insight: Same-color parallel bars define the only valid corridors, so each particle follows a deterministic local trace.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:204:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:205:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:206:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:207:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2b83f449\" lines=\"10-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:208:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:209:Simulate tokens falling through a pipe network after gates rotate open.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:210:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:211:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:212:- Wall (0), bg (pipe fill), gate (horizontal 1×3 bars), token (small edge pixels).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:213:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:214:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:215:- Rotate each gate into a vertical blocker; gate cells become bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:216:- Tokens drop downward through bg, choosing the extreme column for their side (left→min, right→max).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:217:- Tokens settle at true pipe ends (adjacent to wall/boundary), packing inward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:218:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:219:Key insight: Tokens select drop columns by entry side and land at wall-bounded endpoints, ignoring blocker-bounded ones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:220:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:221:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:222:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:223:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\" lines=\"102-115\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:224:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:225:Slide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:226:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:227:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:228:- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:229:- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:230:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:231:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:232:- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:233:- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:234:- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:235:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:236:Key insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:237:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:238:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:239:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:240:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4c416de3\" lines=\"99-118\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:241:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:242:Replicate a pre-drawn corner pattern to every other marker-bearing corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:243:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:244:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:245:- bg = most frequent color. Hollow 0-frames (possibly partial L-shapes); each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:246:  frame-corner cell is either 0 or a painted (non-bg, non-0) color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:247:- >= 1 'source' corner: the pattern is already drawn (one color, both outward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:248:  cells and an inward-diagonal trail).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:249:- Other corners: a single colored pixel on the inward diagonal at the pattern's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:250:  deepest (k,k) offset; the pixel's color is that corner's target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:251:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:252:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:253:- Extract the canonical (TL-oriented) pattern from any source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:254:- For each non-source corner whose marker cell is colored, paint the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:255:  pattern rotated to that corner's orientation, using the marker's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:256:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:257:Key insight: the pattern is symmetric about the corner's inward-diagonal axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:258:(canonical dr == dc), so it reflects cleanly across all four corner orientations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:259:Painting uses each target's OWN marker color, not the source color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:260:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:261:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:262:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:263:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2c181942\" lines=\"7-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:264:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:265:Attach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:266:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:267:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:268:- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:269:- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:270:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:271:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:272:- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:273:- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:274:- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. \n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:275:- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:276:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:277:Key insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:278:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:279:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:280:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:281:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"de809cff\" lines=\"86-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:282:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:283:Turn black dents in two colored regions into marked opposite-color patches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:284:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:285:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:286:- Black background with two large foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:287:- The large regions contain small black dents and a few one-cell color specks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:288:  or protrusions along region boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:289:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:290:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:291:- Locally clean the two foreground regions: isolated specks become black, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:292:  one-cell protrusions surrounded by the other region take that region's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:293:- Each original black dent whose cleaned 3x3 neighborhood is mostly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:294:  foreground color becomes the center of a 3x3 patch in the opposite color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:295:- The dent center itself is recolored teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:296:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:297:Key insight: The teal pixels mark the original black defects; the surrounding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:298:3x3 patch uses the other foreground color, after first removing boundary noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:299:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:300:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:301:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:302:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"cbebaa4b\" lines=\"51-65\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:303:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:304:Assemble scattered jigsaw sprites around a central yellow anchor by pairing red connector pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:305:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:306:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:307:- bg = black (0). Several colored sprites scattered on the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:308:- One anchor sprite contains a 3×3 yellow (4) block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:309:- Each sprite has red (2) connector pixels along its edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:310:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:311:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:312:- The anchor stays in place; remaining sprites attach one at a time.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:313:- Each sprite is translated so that one of its red pixels overlaps an unpaired red pixel on the growing assembly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:314:- Every red connector must pair with exactly one other, forming a complete joined structure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:315:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:316:Key insight: Red pixels act as jigsaw pegs — each must match exactly one counterpart, and the assembly order is determined by which unpaired connectors remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:317:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:318:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:319:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:320:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"c7f57c3e\" lines=\"22-35\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:321:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:322:Swap every sprite to the opposite prototype while preserving scale and position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:323:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:324:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:325:- bg = most common color. Two distinct small sprite patterns (prototypes) appear at various scales.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:326:- Each sprite instance is a scaled copy of one of the two prototypes, placed on the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:327:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:328:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:329:- Identify the two prototype patterns from the smallest-area sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:330:- For each sprite, determine which prototype it matches and its integer scale factor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:331:- Replace it with the other prototype at the same scale, aligned by an internal anchor region (color-1 pixels).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:332:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:333:Key insight: Every sprite toggles to the alternate prototype; the anchor sub-region inside each sprite pins the alignment so swapped sprites land in the correct position regardless of scale.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:334:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:335:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:336:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:337:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"271d71e2\" lines=\"9-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:338:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:339:Move bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:340:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:341:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:342:- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:343:- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:344:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:345:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:346:- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:347:- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:348:- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:349:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:350:Key insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:351:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:352:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:353:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:354:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"898e7135\" lines=\"7-20\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:355:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:356:Inflate a frame's hole-layout and fill each hole with its matching piece.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:357:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:358:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:359:- bg = most common color. Largest component is a monochrome frame enclosing bg holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:360:- Outside pieces composed of k×k blocks; k = side of smallest solid square piece.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:361:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:362:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:363:- Extract connected hole regions inside the frame as slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:364:- Match each piece to a slot by comparing block-level shapes under rotation/flip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:365:- Output the layout scaled by k, with pieces placed in slots; frame color as background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:366:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:367:Key insight: Pieces are k×k-block-scaled versions of holes; downsampling reveals shape matches under all 8 orientations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:368:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:369:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:370:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:371:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:372:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:373:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:374:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:375:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:376:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:377:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:378:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:379:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:380:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:381:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:382:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:383:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:384:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:385:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:386:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:387:请一次性生成 5 个 `<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:388:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:389:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:390:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:391:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:392:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:393:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:394:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:395:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:396:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:397:6. 5 个新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:398:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:399:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:400:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:401:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:402:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:403:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:404:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:405:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:406:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:407:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:408:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:409:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:410:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:411:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:412:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:413:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:414:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:415:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用的复杂计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:416:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:1:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:2:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:3:根据围栏内部种子像素的颜色，从颜色图例中查找对应的填充图案，将该图案平铺填入围栏区域。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:4:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:5:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:6:- 背景色 bg 为网格中最常见的颜色。网格上散布若干由同一颜色构成的封闭围栏（单像素宽的矩形环），每个围栏内部（bg 区域）恰好包含一个非 bg 的单像素\"种子\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:7:- 网格的一条边缘（例如底部两行）是颜色图例区：图例区被 grey 竖线分隔为若干小格，每个小格左上角有一个与某个种子颜色相同的单像素色块，其余部分绘有一个小型二色图案（由该种子颜色和 bg 组成的 2x2 或 3x3 重复单元）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:9:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:10:- 对每个围栏，读取其内部种子像素的颜色 C。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:11:- 在图例区中找到左上角色块颜色为 C 的那个小格，提取其中的重复单元图案 P。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:12:- 将图案 P 以平铺方式填满围栏内部的所有 bg 像素（种子像素本身也被覆盖），平铺的起始对齐点为围栏内部区域的左上角。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:13:- 围栏边框、图例区以及围栏外部的 bg 区域保持不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/des.md:14:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/d